--
--   Description
----------------
--
-- This tests basic transmit functionality in nibble mode at 100Mbits/s.
--
--
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
-- · Checks transmission with all combinations of data code group present
--   within the one frame using 100Mbits/s mode.
-- 
--
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
-- Detailed Test Description
--  1. Initialise suitable wait states for the test.
--  2. Check reset values of registers and setup interrupts
--     and then enable receive in 100M mode into a 32-bit DMA data bus.
--  3. Send several IP frames which have flaws in them so that the checksums
--     should not be checked.
--
-- Test 4.1
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type not 0800 (ARP)
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.2
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type/len = 0x0024, not SNAP (DSAP, 
--    SSAP = 0x5555).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.3
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type/len = 0x0024, not SNAP (Next 2 octets
--    not equal to 0x0300 actually 0x00C0).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.4
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type/len = 0x0024, not SNAP (Next 2 octets 
--    not equal to 0x0000).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.5
--    Broadcast frame, No VLAN, type/len = 0x0024, SNAP but not IP (Next 
--    2 octets not equal to 0x0800).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
-- Test 4.6
--    Broadcast frame, VLAN tag > 4 octets.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.7
--    Broadcast frame, VLAN tag = 4 octets, type/len = 0x0806.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.8
--    Broadcast frame, VLAN tag = 4 octets, type/len = 0x0010, not SNAP.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.9
--    Broadcast frame, Not IPv4 (IPv6 flag in IP header).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.10
--    Broadcast frame, IP header length too short.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.11
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, No VLAN or SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK, 
--    but TOE is disabled in network config register.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.12
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN, no SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK, 
--    but TOE is disabled in network config register.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.13
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN, SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK, 
--    but TOE is disabled in network config register.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.14
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, No VLAN, SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK, 
--    but TOE is disabled in network config register.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.15
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN with CFI, no SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.16
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN with CFI, SNAP, IP and TCP checksums OK.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.17
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (DSAP OK, SSAP bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.18
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (SSAP OK, DSAP bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.19
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (CONTROL OK, ID[7:0] bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.20
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (ID[7:0] OK, CONTROL bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.21
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, no VLAN, bad SNAP (ID[15:8] OK, ID[23:16] bad).
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums not checked (bits [23:22] = 00) and no SNAP (bit 24 low).
-- Test 4.22
--    Broadcast frame, TCP, VLAN, SNAP, good checksum values, to prove we 
--    are setup to accept a good frame.
--    The frame should be copied to memory, with status indicating IP & TCP
--    checksums checked OK (bits [23:22] = 11) and SNAP (bit 24 high).
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 --  check reset state

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbwr      440 88000000  -- write transmit queue pointer 1
